===Etymology 2===
{{ety|en|id=verb|:inh|enm:chekken<ety:der<fro:eschequier<ety:from<eschekier>>>:der<fro:eschec>>|tree=1}}

From {{inh|en|enm|chekken}}, partly from {{der|en|fro|eschequier}} and partly from the noun (see above).

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{sid|en|to inspect}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[inspect]]; to [[examine]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Check''' the oil in your car once a month.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Check''' whether this page has a watermark.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[verify]] the [[accuracy]] of a [[text]] or [[translation]], usually making some [[correction]]s ([[proofread]]) or many ([[copyedit]]).
# {{lb|en|transitive|US|often used with "off"}} To [[mark]] [[item]]s on a [[list]] (with a [[checkmark]] or by [[cross out|crossing them out]]) that have been [[choose|chosen]] for [[keep]]ing or [[removal]] or that have been [[deal with|dealt with]] (for example, [[complete]]d or [[verify|verified]] as [[correct]] or [[satisfactory]]).
#: {{syn|en|check off|tick|q2=UK|tick off|q3=UK|cross off|strike off}}
#: {{ant|en|uncheck}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Check''' the items on the list that interest you.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Check''' the correct answer to each question.}}
# {{sid|en|to limit}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[control]], [[limit]], or [[halt]].
#: {{syn|en|curtail|restrain|Thesaurus:curb}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Check''' your enthusiasm during a negotiation.}}
#: {{ux|en|In mid-sentence, I '''checked''' myself abruptly, looking terribly embarrassed.}}
#* '''c. 1775–1780''', {{w|Edmund Burke}}, ''letter to the Sheriffs of Bristol''
